From 717c7ccf341569a11f6b80d362eaa016285e2b2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 06:44:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: cache flush+invalidate at batch start (A22X)

gl-capture pixel-diff experiments isolated cross-process GPU-side
nondeterminism: 10 consecutive runs of the same deterministic test
program emit byte-identical PM4 cmdstreams (FD_RD_DUMP=enable
confirmed - md5 of all .rd files identical) but produce different
pixel output across runs. Mesa is doing its job; the GPU is producing
different output for byte-identical input.

Issue a CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT at the start of fd2_emit_restore
(right after the existing WFI from 0040), before any state-restore
writes, so each batch starts with the SQ instruction cache and
shader-constant cache flushed regardless of what previous submits
or clients left behind. Cheap once-per-batch. A20X path is unchanged.

NOTE: VS_FETCH_DONE and SC_WAIT_WC events were tried in an earlier
revision of this patch but produced a deterministic 0xc000428b GPUMMU
fault. VS_FETCH_DONE on A2XX uses CP scratch registers
CP_ME_VS_FETCH_DONE_SRC/ADDR/DATA (0x0612-0x0614) for an internal
write; if those scratch regs hold stale or zero values from a prior
context, firing the event makes the CP dereference garbage, which
matches the observed fault address. Drop those two events and rely
on CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT only - it's already used elsewhere in
fd2_draw.c with count=1 and no payload, so it's known-safe.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index 3f500c00a1d..31f45ce3567 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -412,6 +412,26 @@ fd2_emit_restore(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
 
+   /*
+    * Cache flush + invalidate at batch start (A22X only).
+    *
+    * gl-capture pixel-diff experiments showed cross-process GPU-side
+    * nondeterminism on byte-identical PM4 cmdstreams (FD_RD_DUMP md5
+    * identical across runs but pixel output differs). The remaining
+    * source of run-to-run variance is GPU-internal caches retaining
+    * data from a previous submit. CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT drains
+    * the SQ instruction cache and shader-constant cache at batch
+    * start so each batch begins with a clean SQ state regardless
+    * of what previous submits or clients left behind.
+    *
+    * Same event is already used in fd2_draw.c with count=1, so
+    * this is the proven-safe form for A22X.
+    */
+   if (!is_a20x(ctx->screen)) {
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT);
+   }
+
    if (is_a20x(ctx->screen)) {
       OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_RB_BC_CONTROL, 1);
       OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_RB_BC_CONTROL_ACCUM_TIMEOUT_SELECT(3) |
-- 
